Homepage: https://github.com/pioarduino

Package: pioarduino
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
Recommends:
 udev,
# The fork ships the same "platformio" python module, the same pio,
# platformio and piodebuggdb entry points and the same udev rule file as
# platformio itself, so the two cannot be unpacked together. Provides lets a
# package that depends on platformio be satisfied by this one, which is the
# point of a drop-in fork.
Conflicts:
 platformio,
Replaces:
 platformio,
Provides:
 platformio,
Description: PlatformIO fork tracking current Espressif platforms
 pioarduino is the community fork of PlatformIO that keeps up with current
 Espressif platforms - ESP32-C6, ESP32-H2, ESP32-P4 and the Arduino-ESP32 3.x
 cores - which upstream PlatformIO 6.2 does not carry. It is otherwise the
 same build system, and ships the same "pio" and "platformio" command-line
 tools.
 .
 Toolchains, platform definitions and PIO Home are not part of this package:
 they are downloaded into ~/.platformio on first use, per project. The fork
 fetches its own SCons and PIO Home builds from its registry on GitHub rather
 than from platformio.org.
 .
 This package conflicts with platformio: both ship the same module and the
 same entry points. Install one or the other.
